--- a/packages/ws-replication/AGENTS.md
+++ b/packages/ws-replication/AGENTS.md
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ This package implements the Hub/Peer connection and namespace state machines ove
 - Use injected transport, scheduler, randomness, and optional observer/clock seams. Observer or adapter failures must follow their documented isolation and close classifications.
 - Role-specific Cordis plugins consume Instance, Clock, Timer, and Registry services. They own only listener/dialer, replication controller, connections/channels, and their published service; teardown upstream services at the composition root.
 - Keep the edge/session split disciplined (ADR 0032): the seam carries only namespace-domain frames as `Uint8Array` plus the `close`/`terminateUnauthorized`/`settled`/`closed` control signals (and the append-only `connection-fatal` signal); connection-level frames never cross it. Edge validates inbound sequence header-only and stamps outbound sequence at the mux point — sessions encode `sequence=0` placeholders — keeping the wire byte-identical. Append-only for the γ asynchronous seam (ADR 0032 appendix A4, protocol §24): the public `createHubAsyncSessionHost` factory carries session→edge outbound frames as `frame{tag, bytes, lane}` (session-allocated domain tag; the wire sequence is still stamped only at the edge mux point) and adds the edge→session `receipt{tag, sequence}` sequence receipt alongside the existing byte frames and control signals — still no rejection/gate/credit vocabulary, and the β `createHubSessionHost` synchronous freeze stays byte-for-byte untouched. A host assembling the γ asynchronous seam (the `createHubAsyncSessionHost` bridge) **should** set `asyncDataAdmissionFatal: true` on the edge factory — a directional obligation: omitting it silently keeps β semantics (ns-level `send-failed`/ack-timeout resync, connection alive) with zero diagnostics, while setting it on a β synchronous assembly turns data admission overflow from an ns-level resync into connection death. With the marker set, data admission overflow is a connection-fatal (ledger projection overflow → `CONNECTION_BACKPRESSURE` 1011; single frame over the per-connection cap → `FRAME_TOO_LARGE` 1009) with no per-frame rejection, no deferred sends, and no ns-level `send-failed` resync, and the egress pre-gate keeps only the `closed` term (the water-level pause no longer intercepts γ data frames — A4.3/§24.5); the default α/β semantics stay byte-for-byte unchanged.
+- Keep the γ seam's host-side transport duties and two-sided observability discipline explicit when assembling the bridge (protocol §24.2/§24.8; ADR 0032 A4.2/A4.7): the host owns a dedicated FIFO channel pair per (connectionKey, namespaceId) and the receipt clause — the edge stamp return value (egress `sendDataFrame` → wire sequence) must be bridged back into the session's inbound channel as `receipt{tag, sequence}` in the same synchronous segment at the stamp point, ahead of any subsequent socket data; nomicore provides only the stamp return and `HubAsyncSessionHandle.handleReceipt(tag, sequence)`, and receipt-clause violations never degrade silently — an ACK referencing a sequence whose receipt has not been registered fails loudly on the session side (`ACK_STATE_VIOLATION` 1002; violating transport obligations 1–3 is a host bug, §24.2.6). Observability follows fact ownership: `update-sent` and the connection-domain types are observable only through the edge factory `observer` (the rejection-path replicated namespace events `namespace-error{direction: 'sent'}` for authorization refusals, thrown handlers, and openAdmission/no-sink synthesis, plus `namespace-failed{cause: 'open-failed'}`, also observe at the edge); session-domain settlement events (`update-acked`, the chunked family) only through the session host `observer`; cross-thread observer events have no total order, so tests assert per-side facts and causal gates, never merged-array order (reference bridge embodiment: `test/issue447-async-seam.ts`).
 - Keep authorize on the edge side of the seam: edge fully decodes OPEN and calls the injected authorizer; an unauthorized OPEN never crosses the public byte seam, and its wire rejection (`NAMESPACE_UNAUTHORIZED`, refusal latch) is produced by edge-side production code. SessionHost consumes only the settled pre-authorized projection (`localOwner`/`read`/`submit`) and never calls authorize itself.
 - Keep route-key demux O(header): namespace-domain frames expose `namespaceId` at fixed offsets (`UPDATE_CHUNK` shifted by one byte); OPEN full-decodes, ERROR uses a bounded mini-decode, and routing violations reproduce the monolith's two branches (`MALFORMED_FRAME` fatal; sink-less legal frame → synthesized `NAMESPACE_STATE_VIOLATION`). The offset layout is a synchronized-maintenance contract with codec field order, locked by structural guard tests.
 - Keep the two Hub service entrances mutually exclusive: listen mode publishes `nomicoreHubReplication` and never the SessionHost service; exact `listen: false` publishes `nomicoreHubSessionHost` and consumes no `tokens`/`authorization`/`verifyToken`/`authorize` config — authentication and authorization are edge-side duties in that mode. The public factories `createHubReplicationEdge` (a plain factory, not a Cordis plugin, no Registry dependency) and `createHubSessionHost` evolve append-only once published.
